<section class="band-navy" id="how" aria-labelledby="how-title">
  <div class="wrap section">
  <div class="section-head">
    <p class="eyebrow">How it works</p>
    <h2 id="how-title">From published baseline to a plan a person owns</h2>
  </div>
  <ol class="flow" style="--n:5">
    <li><h3>Baseline</h3><p>Start from published APS data, such as APSC employment data, annual-report workforce tables and budget staffing estimates. No agency system needs connecting.</p></li>
    <li><h3>Understand</h3><p>See headcount, skills coverage and AI task exposure by job family, classification and agency.</p></li>
    <li><h3>Forecast</h3><p>Project demand and supply to FY2030 with 50% and 90% uncertainty bands, and see the gap between them.</p></li>
    <li><h3>Test</h3><p>Move the levers planners argue about, such as AI adoption speed, budget growth, attrition and reskilling, and watch outcomes recompute.</p></li>
    <li><h3>Act</h3><p>Generate gap treatments, a risk register, talent pathways and a draft workforce strategy, which a person reviews and owns.</p></li>
  </ol>
  <div class="boundary">
    <div>
      <h3>What the AI does</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Answers questions in plain language through Ask Horizon.</li>
        <li>Drafts strategies, risk registers and narrative reports, grounded and cited on each agency's scorecard.</li>
        <li>Extracts skills from position descriptions, with a confidence score on every match.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="never">
      <h3>What it is built not to do</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Compute a figure:</strong> "The LLM narrates and drafts; it never computes a figure." The analytics produce every number.</li>
        <li><strong>Make the final call:</strong> a planner owns every strategy, treatment and pathway. Low-confidence skills matches queue for human review.</li>
        <li><strong>Send data offshore:</strong> models run on local infrastructure, and no workforce data trains any foundation model.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class="boundary-note">As stated in the Horizon demonstrator.</p>


<h3 class="sub-head">How it is built: four planes, cleanly separated</h3>
  <p class="muted measure">The AI interface is grounded on deterministic analytics, and provenance runs end to end.</p>
  <ol class="planes">
    <li><span><strong>Data plane</strong><span class="plane-sub">Three tiers</span></span>
      <ul class="chips"><li>Tier 1: open and APSC-held data, from day one</li><li>Tier 2: validated agency file extracts</li><li>Tier 3: optional live HR system connectors</li></ul></li>
    <li><span><strong>Analytics plane</strong><span class="plane-sub">Computes every figure</span></span>
      <ul class="chips"><li>Point-in-time workforce model</li><li>Attrition survival models</li><li>Flow forecasting</li><li>Regime detection</li><li>Scenario modelling</li><li>Adjacency matching</li></ul></li>
    <li><span><strong>AI interface plane</strong><span class="plane-sub">Explains and drafts</span></span>
      <ul class="chips"><li>Model gateway, any language model</li><li>Natural-language questions</li><li>Narrative reporting</li><li>Strategy drafting, grounded and cited</li></ul></li>
    <li><span><strong>Hosting plane</strong><span class="plane-sub">Onshore only</span></span>
      <ul class="chips"><li>Australian infrastructure</li><li>Locally hosted models</li><li>Designed with reference to the ISM</li><li>Read-only access</li></ul></li>
  </ol>
  </div>
</section>

