    <div class="acc-set">
      <div class="acc-head">
        <h3>Insight</h3>
        <button type="button" class="btn-text" data-expand-all hidden><span class="js-label">Expand all</span><span class="visually-hidden"> modules</span></button>
      </div>
      <div class="points">
        <details id="horizon-overview"><summary><span class="acc-title">Overview</span><span class="hint">The APS workforce in one view</span></summary><div class="acc-body">
          <p>APS-wide headcount by job family from FY2018 to FY2025, AI task exposure by job family, and headcount by classification.</p>
          <p>FY2025 endpoints are the APSC's published job family shares. Earlier years and the classification view are modelled from published distributions.</p>
        </div></details>
        <details id="horizon-agencies"><summary><span class="acc-title">Agencies</span><span class="hint">Every agency, its own picture</span></summary><div class="acc-body">
          <p>All 102 APS agencies, each with its published headcount at 30 June 2025, a headcount outlook, its job family mix and its sharpest gaps.</p>
          <p>Everything beyond headcount is modelled for the demonstrator. Tier 1 data makes this view possible before any agency system is connected.</p>
        </div></details>
        <details id="horizon-net-impact"><summary><span class="acc-title">Net impact</span><span class="hint">What the AI transition is worth, per agency</span></summary><div class="acc-body">
          <p>What the AI transition is worth to each agency by FY2030 once transition costs are paid, shown as capacity that can be redeployed to priority work. Figures are full-time-equivalent capacity, not positions.</p>
          <p>The model's coefficients are calibrated to cited evidence and are editable assumptions in the platform. See <a href="#data">Data and method</a>.</p>
        </div></details>
        <details id="horizon-skills"><summary><span class="acc-title">Skills inventory</span><span class="hint">A baseline of what the APS can do</span></summary><div class="acc-body">
          <p>A curated skills baseline mapped to the APS Job Family Framework, with coverage by job family, the fastest-moving skills and a check of whether the external market can fill each gap.</p>
          <p>Skills are extracted from position descriptions with a confidence score on each match. Matches below the threshold queue for human review. Extraction from job descriptions, role profiles and learning records comes with the pilot and build phases.</p>
        </div></details>
        <details id="horizon-forecasts"><summary><span class="acc-title">Forecasts</span><span class="hint">Forecasts that admit what they don't know</span></summary><div class="acc-body">
          <p>Demand and supply projected to FY2030 from the published 30 June 2025 baseline, with 50% and 90% uncertainty bands, and the gap between them charted directly.</p>
          <p>Models are validated point-in-time: scored only on data they could not have seen. A detected regime break is marked on the chart.</p>
        </div></details>
        <details id="horizon-labour-market"><summary><span class="acc-title">Labour market</span><span class="hint">The market the APS hires from</span></summary><div class="acc-body">
          <p>APS demand set against national supply, using Jobs and Skills Australia's Occupation Shortage List, Internet Vacancy Index and Employment Projections, education completions, skilled migration and the ACS Digital Pulse.</p>
          <p>Published figures are tagged as published. Everything derived is labelled as modelled, and the weighting behind the contestedness score is stated.</p>
        </div></details>
        <details id="horizon-gaps-risk"><summary><span class="acc-title">Gaps and risk</span><span class="hint">Risks surfaced before they bite</span></summary><div class="acc-body">
          <ul>
            <li>The largest projected skill gaps, ranked by time to impact.</li>
            <li>Single-point dependencies: critical capabilities held by fewer than five people in an agency.</li>
            <li>Options to close each gap across four levers: buy (recruit), build (reskill), borrow (mobility and surge) and bot (automate task content).</li>
            <li>A generated workforce risk register. Planners assign the owners and treatments.</li>
          </ul>
        </div></details>
        <details id="horizon-global"><summary><span class="acc-title">Global context</span><span class="hint">What other governments are doing</span></summary><div class="acc-body">
          <p>How Singapore, the United Kingdom, the United States and OECD guidance compare with Australia, each with the lesson it carries for the APS.</p>
        </div></details>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="acc-set">
      <div class="acc-head"><h3>Plan</h3></div>
      <div class="points">
        <details id="horizon-pathing"><summary><span class="acc-title">Talent pathing</span><span class="hint">Pathways to roles people are close to</span></summary><div class="acc-body">
          <p>Adjacent-skills matching connects people in transforming roles to future-critical roles they are already most of the way to. A pathway is recommended only when its skills-to-train list is short enough to schedule.</p>
          <p>Every recommendation is reviewed by a person before it reaches a conversation with an employee. Aggregated skills-to-train lists can also become a commissioning signal for micro-credentials and graduate streams with university partners.</p>
        </div></details>
        <details id="horizon-scenarios"><summary><span class="acc-title">Scenario workbench</span><span class="hint">Turn the dials, see the decade</span></summary><div class="acc-body">
          <p>Sliders for AI adoption speed, budget growth, attrition and reskilling investment, with outcomes recomputed as the levers move.</p>
          <p>Every saved scenario is stamped with its assumptions and model version, so every run is reproducible and auditable.</p>
        </div></details>
        <details id="horizon-strategy"><summary><span class="acc-title">Strategy generation</span><span class="hint">The strategy layer drafts; the analytics decide</span></summary><div class="acc-body">
          <p>A drafted workforce strategy for each of the 102 agencies, grounded on that agency's own scorecard. A person owns the final document.</p>
          <p>In the demonstrator the drafts are pre-generated. In production they are drafted live through the model gateway on the same grounding.</p>
        </div></details>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="acc-set">
      <div class="acc-head"><h3>Deliver</h3></div>
      <div class="points">
        <details id="horizon-reports"><summary><span class="acc-title">Reports</span><span class="hint">Standard reporting, automated</span></summary><div class="acc-body">
          <p>A whole-of-government AI transition scorecard and a one-page scorecard for each agency, computed from the model, with every figure traceable to its page. Worked examples include a strategic workforce plan extract, a quarterly workforce risk brief and a surge readiness assessment. Everything prints for the executive pack.</p>
        </div></details>
        <details id="horizon-ask"><summary><span class="acc-title">Ask Horizon</span><span class="hint">Questions in plain language, reports on request</span></summary><div class="acc-body">
          <p>A chat interface that draws on the APS dataset, the daily news feed and your own library. Ask for a report, such as "write this up as a Word report", and you get a formatted document with charts, saved to the knowledge base.</p>
          <p>Chat and report generation are part of a free 7-day trial for Australian government agencies.</p>
        </div></details>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="acc-set">
      <div class="acc-head"><h3>Stay informed</h3></div>
