<section class="band-mist" id="trust" aria-labelledby="trust-title">
  <div class="wrap section">
    <div class="section-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Trust and security</p>
      <h2 id="trust-title">Hosted in Australia, with locally hosted models</h2>
      <p>As stated in the demonstrator's platform and hosting section, your data and the models that read it stay onshore.</p>
    </div>
    <dl class="facts facts--icons">
      <div><dt class="ic ic--server">Hosting</dt><dd>Infrastructure in Australia. Data never leaves the country.</dd></div>
      <div><dt class="ic ic--cpu">Models</dt><dd>Locally hosted open-weights models by default, with GovAI-hosted models as an option as they roll out. No offshore processing.</dd></div>
      <div><dt class="ic ic--lock">Training</dt><dd>No workforce data is used to train any foundation model.</dd></div>
      <div><dt class="ic ic--cloud">Deployment</dt><dd>Horizon's Australian-hosted software as a service, or deployment into an agency-owned cloud subscription where the Commonwealth keeps data custody.</dd></div>
      <div><dt class="ic ic--key">Access</dt><dd>Read-only against every source system. Agency single sign-on is planned for the build phase.</dd></div>
      <div><dt class="ic ic--shield">Controls</dt><dd>Designed with reference to the Information Security Manual (ISM).</dd></div>
      <div><dt class="ic ic--sliders">Bias</dt><dd>Subgroup audits ship with every retraining cycle.</dd></div>
    </dl>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="wrap section" id="questions" aria-labelledby="questions-title">
  <div data-acc-scope>
    <div class="acc-head">
      <h2 id="questions-title">Common questions</h2>
      <button type="button" class="btn-text" data-expand-all hidden><span class="js-label">Expand all</span><span class="visually-hidden"> questions</span></button>
    </div>
    <div class="points">
      <details id="q-hz-connect"><summary><span class="acc-title">Do we need to connect our HR system to start?</span></summary><div class="acc-body"><p>No. Published Tier 1 data gives a useful picture from day one, with no agency work. Validated file extracts and optional live connectors deepen it over time.</p></div></details>
      <details id="q-hz-real"><summary><span class="acc-title">Which figures are real and which are modelled?</span></summary><div class="acc-body"><p>The APSC's published figures are the real baseline, such as headcount, agencies, locations and the separation rate. Record-level detail, histories, forecasts and impact figures are modelled from published data, and every one is labelled as modelled.</p></div></details>
      <details id="q-hz-ai-numbers"><summary><span class="acc-title">Does the AI produce the numbers?</span></summary><div class="acc-body"><p>No. The analytics compute every figure. The language model narrates and drafts, grounded and cited on those figures.</p></div></details>
      <details id="q-hz-data"><summary><span class="acc-title">Where does our workforce data go?</span></summary><div class="acc-body"><p>It stays in Australia. Horizon runs on Australian infrastructure with locally hosted models, can be deployed into your own cloud subscription, reads source systems read-only, and never uses workforce data to train a foundation model.</p></div></details>
      <details id="q-hz-cuts"><summary><span class="acc-title">Is this about cutting staff?</span></summary><div class="acc-body"><p>Horizon does not model redundancies. It measures capacity that can be redeployed to priority work. In its modelling, any fall in headcount comes through natural separations, or the capacity absorbs new demand without growth. How an agency uses that capacity is its own decision.</p></div></details>
      <details id="q-hz-try"><summary><span class="acc-title">Can we try it?</span></summary><div class="acc-body"><p>Yes. The demonstrator is public. Chat and report generation are part of a free 7-day trial for Australian government agencies.</p></div></details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

